IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa7-ch7.l4: Part 13 Chapter 7, Supplementary provisions (ss 360 to 361), with ss 360A to 360C, lines 4598-4655 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4.
-- This module comes before the others because the clear day rule of s 360(2) is called by Chapter 3 and Chapter 4.

§ `Part 13 Chapter 7 -- Supplementary provisions`

-- ---- s 360 Computation of periods of notice etc: clear day rule --------------------------------------------

-- The provisions listed in s 360(1), as the text names them (a provision is named by the text's own string).
-- src:4600 | (1) This section applies for the purposes of the following provisions of this Part—
-- src:4601 | section 307(1) and (2) (notice required of general meeting),
-- src:4602 | section 307A(1), (4), (5) and (7)(b) (notice required of general meeting of traded company),
-- src:4603 | section 312(1) and (3) (resolution requiring special notice),
-- src:4604 | section 314(4)(d) (request to circulate members' statement),
-- src:4605 | section 316(2)(b) (expenses of circulating statement to be deposited or tendered before meeting),
-- src:4606 | section 337(3) (contents of notice of AGM of traded company),
-- src:4607 | section 338(4)(d)(i) (request to circulate member's resolution at AGM of public company),. . .
-- src:4608 | section 338A(5) (request to include matter in the business to be dealt with at AGM of traded company),
-- src:4609 | section 340(2)(b)(i) (expenses of circulating statement to be deposited or tendered before meeting), and
-- src:4610 | section 340B(2)(b) (traded companies: duty to circulate members' matters for AGM).
@ref s 360(1) Computation of periods of notice etc: the provisions to which the clear day rule applies (src:4600-4610)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(1) the clear day rule applies for the purposes of the provision` MEANS
    IF elem provision
        (LIST "section 307(1) and (2)"
              "section 307A(1), (4), (5) and (7)(b)"
              "section 312(1) and (3)"
              "section 314(4)(d)"
              "section 316(2)(b)"
              "section 337(3)"
              "section 338(4)(d)(i)"
              "section 338A(5)"
              "section 340(2)(b)(i)"
              "section 340B(2)(b)")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section applies for the purposes of the following provisions of this Part" does not say "only"

-- The clear days between two days exclude both: the day on which the notice is given (or the request received or the
-- sum deposited or tendered) and the day of the meeting.
-- src:4611 | (2) Any reference in those provisions to a period of notice, or to a period before a meeting by which a request must be received or sum deposited or tendered, is to a period of the specified length excluding—
-- src:4612 | (a) the day of the meeting, and
-- src:4613 | (b) the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered.
@ref s 360(2) Computation of periods of notice etc: the days excluded (src:4611-4613)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 360(2) the clear days between the day the notice is given and the day of the meeting` MEANS
    (`the day of the meeting` MINUS `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered`) MINUS 1

@ref s 360(2) Computation of periods of notice etc: a period of the specified length (src:4611-4613)
GIVEN `the length of the period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(2) the period of the specified length is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 360(2) the clear days between the day the notice is given and the day of the meeting` `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered` `the day of the meeting` AT LEAST `the length of the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to a period of the specified length excluding— (a) the day of the meeting, and (b) the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered" -- MARGINAL a

-- ---- s 360A Electronic meetings and voting -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4615 | (1) Nothing in this Part is to be taken to preclude the holding and conducting of a meeting in such a way that persons who are not present together at the same place may by electronic means attend and speak and vote at it.
@ref s 360A(1) Electronic meetings and voting (src:4615)
GIVEN `persons who are not present together at the same place attend, speak and vote at the meeting by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360A(1) this Part precludes the holding and conducting of the meeting in that way` MEANS
    IF `persons who are not present together at the same place attend, speak and vote at the meeting by electronic means`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Part is to be taken to preclude the holding and conducting of a meeting in such a way that persons who are not present together at the same place may by electronic means attend and speak and vote at it"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of meetings held in that way

-- src:4616 | (2) In the case of a traded company the use of electronic means for the purpose of enabling members to participate in a general meeting may be made subject only to such requirements and restrictions as are—
-- src:4617 | (a) necessary to ensure the identification of those taking part and the security of the electronic communication, and
-- src:4618 | (b) proportionate to the achievement of those objectives.
@ref s 360A(2) Electronic meetings and voting: traded companies (src:4616-4618)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement or restriction is necessary to ensure the identification of those taking part and the security of the electronic communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement or restriction is proportionate to the achievement of those objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360A(2) the use of electronic means may be made subject to the requirement or restriction` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a traded company"
    ELSE IF `the requirement or restriction is necessary to ensure the identification of those taking part and the security of the electronic communication`
            AND `the requirement or restriction is proportionate to the achievement of those objectives`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made subject only to such requirements and restrictions as are— (a) necessary ... and (b) proportionate" -- FORK F11

-- src:4619 | (3) Nothing in subsection (2) affects any power of a company to require reasonable evidence of the entitlement of any person who is not a member to participate in the meeting.
@ref s 360A(3) Electronic meetings and voting: evidence of entitlement (src:4619)
GIVEN `the person is not a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360A(3) subsection (2) affects the company's power to require reasonable evidence of entitlement` MEANS
    IF `the person is not a member`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (2) affects any power of a company to require reasonable evidence of the entitlement of any person who is not a member to participate in the meeting"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who is not a member"

-- ---- s 360AA Traded companies: confirmation of receipt of electronic voting --------------------------------

DECLARE `s 360AA(1) who cast the vote` IS ONE OF
    `s 360AA(1)(a) the member`
    `s 360AA(1)(b) the proxy`
    `s 360AA(1)(c) the representative of a corporation under section 323(1)`

-- src:4621 | (1) In the case of a traded company, where a vote is cast on a poll by electronic means the company must ensure that, as soon as reasonably practicable after the vote has been received, confirmation of receipt of the vote is sent by electronic means to—
-- src:4622 | (a) the member, where that person cast the vote,
-- src:4623 | (b) the proxy, where the vote was cast by proxy, or
-- src:4624 | (c) the representative, where the vote was cast by a person authorised to act as a representative of a corporation in accordance with section 323(1).
@ref s 360AA(1) Traded companies: confirmation of receipt of electronic voting (src:4621-4624)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote is cast on a poll by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who cast the vote` IS A `s 360AA(1) who cast the vote`
      `confirmation of receipt was sent by electronic means to that person as soon as reasonably practicable after the vote was received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360AA(1) the company has sent confirmation of receipt of the vote` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`) OR (NOT `the vote is cast on a poll by electronic means`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a traded company, where a vote is cast on a poll by electronic means"
    ELSE IF `confirmation of receipt was sent by electronic means to that person as soon as reasonably practicable after the vote was received`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must ensure that, as soon as reasonably practicable after the vote has been received, confirmation of receipt of the vote is sent by electronic means" -- FORK F5

DECLARE `s 360AA(2) where the vote is cast` IS ONE OF
    `s 360AA(2)(a) at a meeting`
    `s 360AA(2)(b) at an electronic meeting conducted in accordance with section 360A`
    `s 360AA(2)(c) in advance of a meeting or electronic meeting (see section 322A)`
    `s 360AA(2) somewhere else`

-- src:4625 | (2) A vote under subsection (1) includes any vote cast—
-- src:4626 | (a) at a meeting;
-- src:4627 | (b) at an electronic meeting conducted in accordance with section 360A;
-- src:4628 | (c) in advance of a meeting or electronic meeting (see section 322A).
@ref s 360AA(2) Traded companies: confirmation of receipt of electronic voting: the votes covered (src:4625-4628)
GIVEN `where the vote is cast` IS A `s 360AA(2) where the vote is cast`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360AA(2) the vote is a vote under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the vote is cast`
    WHEN `s 360AA(2) somewhere else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "A vote under subsection (1) includes any vote cast"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 360B Traded companies: requirements for participating in and voting at general meetings -------------

-- "No account is to be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day": the hours that count are the hours of the
-- period less the hours of it that fall on a day that is not a working day.
-- src:4634 | (3) In calculating the period mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (2), no account is to be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day.
@ref s 360B(3) Traded companies: calculating the period (src:4634)
GIVEN `hours in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 360B(3) the hours of the period that are counted` MEANS
    `hours in the period` MINUS `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day`

-- src:4631 | (a) imposing a restriction on a right of a member to participate in and vote at a general meeting of the company unless the member's shares have (after having been acquired by the member and before the meeting) been deposited with, or transferred to, or registered in the name of another person, or
@ref s 360B(1)(a) Traded companies: restriction on the right to participate and vote (src:4631)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision imposes a restriction on a member's right to participate in and vote at a general meeting unless the member's shares have, after being acquired and before the meeting, been deposited with, transferred to or registered in the name of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360B(1)(a) the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    IF `the company is a traded company`
        AND `the provision imposes a restriction on a member's right to participate in and vote at a general meeting unless the member's shares have, after being acquired and before the meeting, been deposited with, transferred to or registered in the name of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of"

-- src:4632 | (b) imposing a restriction on the right of a member to transfer shares in the company during the period of 48 hours before the time for the holding of a general meeting of the company if that right would not otherwise be subject to that restriction.
@ref s 360B(1)(b) Traded companies: restriction on transfer before a meeting (src:4632)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision restricts the right to transfer shares during the 48 hours (counting only working-day time) before the time for holding a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right would not otherwise be subject to that restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360B(1)(b) the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    IF `the company is a traded company`
        AND `the provision restricts the right to transfer shares during the 48 hours (counting only working-day time) before the time for holding a general meeting`
        AND `the right would not otherwise be subject to that restriction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of"

-- src:4633 | (2) A traded company must determine the right to vote at a general meeting of the company by reference to the register of members as at a time (determined by the company) that is not more than 48 hours before the time for the holding of the meeting.
@ref s 360B(2) Traded companies: the time for determining the right to vote (src:4633)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours before the time for holding the meeting at which the register of members was taken as the basis of the right to vote` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of that period that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360B(2) the time determined by the company is one this subsection allows` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A traded company must determine the right to vote"
    ELSE IF `s 360B(3) the hours of the period that are counted` `hours before the time for holding the meeting at which the register of members was taken as the basis of the right to vote` `hours of that period that fall on a day that is not a working day` AT MOST 48
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by reference to the register of members as at a time (determined by the company) that is not more than 48 hours before the time for holding of the meeting"

DECLARE `s 360B(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 360B(4)(a)(i) the operation of Part 22 of this Act (information about interests in a company's shares)`
    `s 360B(4)(a)(ii) the operation of Part 15 of the Companies Act 1985 (orders imposing restrictions on shares)`
    `s 360B(4)(a)(iii) any provision in a company's articles relating to the application of any provision of either of those Parts`
    `s 360B(4)(b) the validity of articles prescribed, or to the same effect as articles prescribed, under section 19 of this Act`
    `s 360B(4) another matter`

-- src:4635 | (4) Nothing in this section affects—
-- src:4636 | (a) the operation of—
-- src:4637 | (i) Part 22 of this Act (information about interests in a company's shares),
-- src:4638 | (ii) Part 15 of the Companies Act 1985 (orders imposing restrictions on shares), or
-- src:4639 | (iii) any provision in a company's articles relating to the application of any provision of either of those Parts; or
-- src:4640 | (b) the validity of articles prescribed, or to the same effect as articles prescribed, under section 19 of this Act (power of Secretary of State to prescribe model articles).
@ref s 360B(4) Traded companies: saving (src:4635-4640)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 360B(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360B(4) this section does not affect the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 360B(4) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section affects— (a) ... (b) ..."
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 360BA Traded companies: right to confirmation of vote after a general meeting -----------------------

-- src:4645 | (a) the member makes a request for the information, which request is received by the company no later than 30 days from the date of that general meeting, and
@ref s 360BA(2)(a) Traded companies: right to confirmation of vote: the request (src:4645)
GIVEN `the date of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the member's request was received by the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360BA(2)(a) the request was received in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the member's request was received by the company` AT MOST `the date of the general meeting` PLUS 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which request is received by the company no later than 30 days from the date of that general meeting" -- FORK F7

-- src:4646 | (b) the member does not have any other reasonable means by which to determine that their vote has been validly recorded and counted by the company.
@ref s 360BA(2)(b) Traded companies: right to confirmation of vote: no other means (src:4646)
GIVEN `the member has another reasonable means by which to determine that their vote has been validly recorded and counted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360BA(2)(b) the member has no other reasonable means` MEANS
    IF `the member has another reasonable means by which to determine that their vote has been validly recorded and counted`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the member does not have any other reasonable means by which to determine that their vote has been validly recorded and counted by the company"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4643 | (1) Where the conditions in subsection (2) are met, a traded company must provide information to a member which enables the member to confirm that their vote on a resolution at a general meeting where a poll has been taken has been validly recorded and counted.
-- src:4644 | (2) The conditions are that—
-- src:4645 | (a) the member makes a request for the information, which request is received by the company no later than 30 days from the date of that general meeting, and
-- src:4646 | (b) the member does not have any other reasonable means by which to determine that their vote has been validly recorded and counted by the company.
@ref s 360BA(1) Traded companies: right to confirmation of vote after a general meeting (src:4643-4646)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a poll has been taken on the resolution at the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 360BA(2)(a) the request was received in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 360BA(2)(b) the member has no other reasonable means` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360BA(1) the company must provide the information to the member` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`) OR (NOT `a poll has been taken on the resolution at the general meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a traded company must provide information to a member ... a resolution at a general meeting where a poll has been taken"
    ELSE IF `s 360BA(2)(a) the request was received in time` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 360BA(2)(b) the member has no other reasonable means` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `s 360BA(2)(a) the request was received in time` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 360BA(2)(b) the member has no other reasonable means` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the conditions in subsection (2) are met" -- MARGINAL a
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known

-- The period of 15 days begins with the later of the two first working days, so it ends 14 days after that day.
-- src:4647 | (3) The information under subsection (1) must be provided to the member as soon as reasonably practicable and in any event by the end of the period of 15 days beginning with whichever is the later of the first working day after the day on which—
-- src:4648 | (a) the result of the poll is declared for that resolution; or
-- src:4649 | (b) the request for information under subsection (2)(a) is received by the company.
@ref s 360BA(3) Traded companies: right to confirmation of vote: the last day (src:4647-4649)
GIVEN `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared for the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the first working day after the day on which the request is received by the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 360BA(3) the last day for providing the information` MEANS
    IF `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared for the resolution` AT LEAST `the first working day after the day on which the request is received by the company`
    THEN `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared for the resolution` PLUS 14
    ELSE `the first working day after the day on which the request is received by the company` PLUS 14

@ref s 360BA(3) Traded companies: right to confirmation of vote: in time (src:4647-4649)
GIVEN `the last day for providing the information` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the information was provided` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360BA(3) the information was provided in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the information was provided` AT MOST `the last day for providing the information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event by the end of the period of 15 days beginning with whichever is the later" -- FORK F7

-- ---- s 360C Meaning of "traded company" -------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 360C class of shares` HAS
    `carries rights to vote at general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market by or with the consent of the company` IS A BOOLEAN

-- This is the seam answer other parts take as `s 360C the company is a traded company`.
-- src:4651 | In this Part, “ traded company ” means a company any shares of which—
-- src:4652 | (a) carry rights to vote at general meetings, and
-- src:4653 | (b) are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market by or with the consent of the company.
@ref s 360C Meaning of "traded company" (src:4651-4653)
GIVEN `the company's shares, by class or holding` IS A LIST OF `s 360C class of shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360C the company is a traded company` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN shares YIELD shares's `carries rights to vote at general meetings`
                AND shares's `admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market by or with the consent of the company`)
           `the company's shares, by class or holding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“traded company” means a company any shares of which— (a) carry rights to vote at general meetings, and (b) are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market by or with the consent of the company"

-- ---- s 361 Meaning of "quoted company" ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Quoted company" in this Part has the meaning it has in Part 15 (s 385, coa8): the answer is taken as an input.
-- src:4655 | In this Part “quoted company” has the same meaning as in Part 15 of this Act.
@ref s 361 Meaning of "quoted company" (src:4655)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361 the company is a quoted company` MEANS
    `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
